<</AP<</N 21230 0 R >>/C[ 1 0.941177 0.4]/CA 1/Contents(A polygene is a member of a group of non-epistatic genes that interact additively to influence a phenotypic trait, thus contributing to multiple-gene inheritance, a type of non-Mendelian inheritance, as opposed to single-gene inheritance, which is the core notion of Mendelian inheritance. The term "monozygous" is usually used to refer to a hypothetical gene as it is often difficult to distinguish the effect of an individual gene from the effects of other genes)/F 4/PDFIUM_HasGeneratedAP true/Popup 21229 0 R /QuadPoints[ 280 406.25 327 406.25 280 394.25 327 394.25]/Rect[ 280 394.25 327 406.25]/Subtype/Highlight/Type/Annot>>
